Package: powerkit
Title: Unified Power Analysis for Psychology Designs
Version: 0.14.1
Authors@R:
    person("Joel", "Thornton", , "58643641+JoelThornton@users.noreply.github.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Reads a single design specification (JSON) for common
    psychology designs, checks that it describes a possible population, and
    routes it to validated backends ('pwr', 'Spower', 'power4mome',
    'Superpower', 'InteractionPoweR') to estimate power, required sample size
    and sensitivity. This development version runs basic tests (by exact
    formula via 'pwr', or simulation via 'Spower'), 2x2 between and 2x2
    mixed ANOVA designs (via Superpower),
    two-way regression interactions (via InteractionPoweR), and simple,
    parallel and serial mediation and first- and second-stage moderated
    mediation (PROCESS models 4, 6, 7 and 14, via power4mome),
    cluster-randomised trials (via 'powertools'), and the fit of structural
    equation models (via 'semPower').
